{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544814-some-hopefully-constructive-criticism-of-curseborne","id":1544814,"title":"Some (hopefully) Constructive Criticism of Curseborne","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-26T14:15:20-07:00","id":1544814,"title":"Some (hopefully) Constructive Criticism of Curseborne","content":"I've posted these on the Kickstarter comments, but wanted to come directly to the forum and place them more deliberately and get input from others.<br /> <br /> Let me start this off by saying, I really like Curseborne so far, and it's a game I definitely want to run. It has a ton of awesome story possibilities and great Roleplay. I'm also happy the Kickstarter has been so successful for Onyx Path, as personally and rather bluntly... I see them as having been robbed of their own original creations. Which really sucks. So Curseborne being a spiritual successor, a success, and bringing in a ton of new ideas that are a lot of fun is overall just awesome.<br /> <br /> But....<br /> <br /> Based off of the manuscript readings I've done, I still have some nitpicks and personal concerns for the game. Personal concerns that will if not addressed, see me basically writing a small document of &quot;House rules and abilities&quot; for my own table to really make the game into something I want...And I'd much rather prefer Onyx Path address these issues themselves so I'm not running my own version of Curseborne that is 25% my own rules meaning people coming to play with me might take umbrage and future Curseborne supplements become less useful, yadda, yadda.<br /> <br /> Anyway, let me get to the point.<br /> <br /> A couple years ago, I started writing my own &quot;World of Darkness Heartbreaker.&quot; I was calling 'Children of the Night'. The long and short of it is, it looked a lot like Curseborne in concept, Multiple Supernatural Creatures, all with their unique inherent abilities... But sharing a Master Power List with different creatures having discounts/unique uses of that Master Power List. <br /> <br /> So yeah, clearly I love Curseborne since myself (and I assume lots of other gamers) have had similar ideas.<br /> <br /> My issues for Curseborne, however, primarily have to deal with... well the &quot;Super&quot; of the Supernatural... some of the powers and abilities, some that seem missing, and some that seem like they can be improved.<br /> <br /> So let's start right away with Lineages and the one that sticks in my craw as needing the most work, Primals and their Wild Form.<br /> <br /> Right now, the Wild Form is quite frankly.... very underwhelming. There's absolutely no difference in the Wild Form when comparing a Lykan to a Hyde to a Vodnick except for how you describe it.<br /> <br /> And while that might be enough for people who don't care about game Mechanics and favor fiction entirely, I'm not here to play FATE or Powered by the Apocalypse. (Nothing wrong with those games, but they don't scratch the itch for this genre) Quite frankly, I want the ability for players to give some amount of customization to their Wild Form.<br /> <br /> Lykans don't have claws and teeth..... Vodnicks aren't amphibious. One is a Werewolf, one is a Frogman/Deep One.... Yet mechanically they are exactly the same. Just as the Hyde is exactly the same.<br /> <br /> The only way they can get say, gills, or wings, or claws, or teeth... Is to buy the Practices that allow them to transform... <br /> <br /> And that doesn't feel like a person with a set &quot;Wild Form&quot; to me... it feels more like a Lunar from Exalted who buys charms for all the different Shape Shifting tricks they want.<br /> <br /> My own personal solution to this would be to give a small pool of customization points and let a Primal Player more or less &quot;Build&quot; their wild Form. You don't have to go crazy with it... But just having something like...<br /> <br /> *Weapon Tags for Natural Weapons like Claws, Teeth, Horns<br /> *Enhanced Senses to give Enhancements on certain checks, star light vision, blood hound nose, cat hearing,<br /> *Aquatic Adaption<br /> *Increased Movement<br /> *Inherent Armor<br /> *Increased Physical Stats<br /> <br /> Yes, there are Practices that do a lot of these things, but you don't need to make the Wild Form versions as powerful as the Practice. Let them stack with the various different spells of the Practices and the Wild Form's abilities become even greater. You could give an *Average* wild form build for every family and still let players customize to really make their Form unique, important and a feature of playing a Primal.<br /> <br /> Now in brief, the other things I wanted to see addressed were<br /> *More detailed info on how Feeding Works, since just saying &quot;They eat Memories&quot; is vague and unhelpful when there's literally a power designed for wiping memories and it would really suck if Ascetics feeding is more powerful or as versatile as the Entanglement 4 version of the Memory wiping power.<br /> <br /> *The lack of ability for creating zombies.<br /> We know Zombies are in the game. Why can't anyone make Undead Servitors? Multiple Splats in CoD and WoD were capable of this right out of the gate. Honestly there are a few Spells across all of the Practices that seem like they could be grouped together into a &quot;Necromancy&quot; Power Set... throw in the ability to create Undead with it, and it would be perfect.<br /> <br /> *There is no ability to gain Enhanced Strength unless you are &quot;Hungry&quot;<br /> There's no power right now that increases your Strength. No ability to have actual supernatural strength. Lots of &quot;Do more damage with your attack.&quot; But going back to Primals in particular, and most likely some Outcasts and the Dead... why don't we have any ability for them to become strong enough to start flipping cars and throwing manhole covers around? It's a thematic thing that's probably even more important than the Necromancy thing.<br /> <br /> Anyway that's what is on my mind. I still love this game and most everything about it, but these stand out to me right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-26T15:04:16-07:00","id":1544815,"title":"","content":"I either fully or partly agree with pretty much all of this.<br /> <br /> I do think that an intended part of the game design is that some things are left up to individual Storyguides and I don't think that's an inherently bad thing but I'd like a lot more clarity on the kind of leeway that SGs have to make calls on this kind of thing and, perhaps more importantly, what kinds of things it's acceptable for players to ask their Storyguides for.<br /> <br /> Primal Wild Forms vs Hungry Feeding Preferences are perhaps the clearest example of the two extremes that coexist in the game here.<br /> <br /> The game mechanical effects of a Primal Wild Form are highly concretised while also being fairly minimal: you get a +1 Enhancement that stacks to physical actions while transformed and that's it. There's no indication that you're allowed to ask for or give any other kinds of abilities that might be appropriate and indeed quite a lot of abilities are actively gated behind Inheritances (like Vodnik water breathing) or Spells (like Lykans tracking by scent).<br /> <br /> By contrast Hungry seem to just be able to grant themselves quite potent supernatural powers merely by having that power described as their &quot;feeding preference&quot;. Vorare straight up get the ability to consume souls. Black Hearts get the power to drain emotions. Ascetics get a memory-draining ability that from the flavour text seems more effective than the Tabula Rasa spell.<br /> <br /> Possibly the intent is that in both cases the SG has wide leeway to grant mechanical benefits to players but that in no way comes across in the Primal chapter, or anywhere else in the book. If the SG is meant to say &quot;yeah of course you get Power Advantage on that attempt to flip a car, you're a freakin' werewolf&quot; it isn't *mentioned* anywhere. Unlike the OP I don't mind if these things aren't nailed down but I *do* want them to be explored. Right now the manuscript contains a lot of unreliable narration and very little explanation.<br /> <br /> I know Danielle has said she thinks a lot of these issues can be addressed with small sidebars but I think they might actually need some *quite large* sidebars and preferably a good number of examples spread throughout the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-26T17:16:51-07:00","id":1544821,"title":"","content":"I agree with all I read, and honestly didn\u2019t back it for these among other things I expected from a NNWoD.<br /> <br /> One thing I must add is that I disagree on the Zombi thing. I think there are things that don\u2019t need to be described as spells, but as rituals. Honestly there is no Zombi ritual written, but it fits perfectly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-26T17:22:14-07:00","id":1544823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544814-some-hopefully-constructive-criticism-of-curseborne?p=1544821#post1544821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with all I read, and honestly didn\u2019t back it for these among other things I expected from a NNWoD.<br /> <br /> One thing I must add is that I disagree on the Zombi thing. I think there are things that don\u2019t need to be described as spells, but as rituals. Honestly there is no Zombi ritual written, but it fits perfectly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the Zombie thing doesn't bother me so much, I agree that it's best handled as rituals.<br /> <br /> I do think the lack of any real way to do Necromancy at all, even spirit-focused Necromancy, despite multiple Families explicitly being necromancers, is kind of more of a big deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28625,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","user":"Nobody Special","date":". 10-26-2024, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-27T09:56:27-07:00","id":1544849,"title":"","content":"I agree one some of these points. Though when it comes, for example, to Primals when the shift forms, the specific powers are kinda linked to the spells that they choose. For example, Force of Nature can represent natural weapons. Impenetrable Skin could represent large size, extreme toughness, natural weapons, etc. <br /> <br /> I would like expanded necromancy magic. I liked V20 Necromancy with the various paths. That is something that could potentially be introduced in future books, along with a variety of other spells to flesh out character options. Enhancing physical attributes could be in that category as well.<br /> <br /> One thing I think that needs to be cleaned up is ways to regain Curse Dice. How do the Hungry drain emotions, memories, or souls? How much can the Hungry drain? What are the effects on the victims. We know that some Hungry are going to want a lot of Curse Dice from feeding - how much can be drained from the victim and when do they die from it? Sorcerer sacrifices could potentially be in this category as well - can I just burn a $100 bill and get a Curse Die?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-27T12:49:55-07:00","id":1544864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544814-some-hopefully-constructive-criticism-of-curseborne?p=1544849#post1544849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree one some of these points. Though when it comes, for example, to Primals when the shift forms, the specific powers are kinda linked to the spells that they choose. For example, Force of Nature can represent natural weapons. Impenetrable Skin could represent large size, extreme toughness, natural weapons, etc.<br /> <br /> I would like expanded necromancy magic. I liked V20 Necromancy with the various paths. That is something that could potentially be introduced in future books, along with a variety of other spells to flesh out character options. Enhancing physical attributes could be in that category as well.<br /> <br /> One thing I think that needs to be cleaned up is ways to regain Curse Dice. How do the Hungry drain emotions, memories, or souls? How much can the Hungry drain? What are the effects on the victims. We know that some Hungry are going to want a lot of Curse Dice from feeding - how much can be drained from the victim and when do they die from it? Sorcerer sacrifices could potentially be in this category as well - can I just burn a $100 bill and get a Curse Die?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that Spells, especially Mutable Form spells are currently what's meant to do the job of customising your Wild Form, the problem is that they aren't currently tied to it. If my Werewolf gives herself claws and Force of Nature, that's already two CD bled and activating Wild Form costs a third for no significant benefit. <br /> <br /> This could resolved be solved by letting Primals reflexively cast self-buffing spells on themselves for free when they enter Wild Form but that might not do much if it's restricted to Mutable Form or else do too much if it's, like &quot;any physical spell that targets yourself&quot; (although having said that plenty of Families get to cast Physical spells for free anyway) and that would probably be the most elegant solution.<br /> <br /> As for vampires and sorcerers, the intent here seems to be that you have to spend a full scene doing the thing for it to count. The problem is that this seems different if you're talking about the dice for Feeding/Sacrifices vs if you're taking any the dice for Damnation resolution. <br /> <br /> I will say that in this regard it's a specific case of a more general issue which is that *every* way a character generates Curse Dice ultimately relies on a GM call and that isn't necessarily a deal breaker. Deciding if somebody counts as feeding or sacrificing meaningfully is ultimately no harder than deciding if &quot;the whole crew came together to solve a problem&quot; or if somebody &quot;exemplified their family themes&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Primal Damnation is actually a really good example for how this can be made a little more concrete in that it explicitly lists Conditions you have to inflict on somebody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-27T13:20:25-07:00","id":1544866,"title":"","content":"Casting self buffs on themselves for free when they transform makes a lot of sense. They already are bleeding a curse die to change.<br /> <br /> Currently, the Spawn of Vodnik are the only Primal that can bleed one fewer CD for physical spells. In fact they need to hold one less CD too, so that is a huge advantage for them with numerous Primal spells which are physical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 10-27-2024, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-02T14:26:30-07:00","id":1545223,"title":"","content":"I have some questionable points about the Hungry.<br /> <br /> * It was clarified in a forum post but I don't think the actual manuscript says whether or not <b>The Hungry</b> get fangs when they become undead. Obviously, this is an iconic part of vampiredom but I think should be written up.<br /> <br /> * Do these fangs have an affect similar to <b>The Kiss</b> or not? It probably should and maybe an amnesiac effect or not but in a lot of non-WOD vampire lore, vampire attacks are just horrifying and traumatizing until you brainwash them afterward to forget or leave them dead.<br /> <br /> * Do the Hungry have anything similar to<b> ghouls</b> or is it like Blade or What We Do In the Shadows that human servants work for cash or the promise of becoming undead themselves? Do they employ other Accursed in this role or what?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-02T15:44:13-07:00","id":1545227,"title":"","content":"While I agree more clarity is a good thing, a couple of notes on the Ghoul thing:<br /> <br /> There's an Advance for Vital Flow that's specifically called &quot;Ghoul&quot; but it only lasts until the end of the story. <br /> <br /> Drones from the Adversay section are implied to be created sometimes when vampires feed and to act as servants to various supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-02T16:43:53-07:00","id":1545230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544814-some-hopefully-constructive-criticism-of-curseborne?p=1545227#post1545227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree more clarity is a good thing, a couple of notes on the Ghoul thing:<br /> <br /> There's an Advance for Vital Flow that's specifically called &quot;Ghoul&quot; but it only lasts until the end of the story.<br /> <br /> Drones from the Adversay section are implied to be created sometimes when vampires feed and to act as servants to various supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I feel more detail would be useful for this because it's things players are likely to do rather than just NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-02T16:56:03-07:00","id":1545234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544814-some-hopefully-constructive-criticism-of-curseborne?p=1545230#post1545230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I feel more detail would be useful for this because it's things players are likely to do rather than just NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the way the devs are talking I feel like having Drone servants is very much in the &quot;beyond the scope of Entanglement 1-4&quot; box.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T12:55:15-08:00","id":1545336,"title":"","content":"After rereading the texts, my thoughts<br /> <br /> -god I thought the cofd books were &quot;dry&quot; by the absence of IC narration, but it must have been nostalgia giving me rose tinted glasses. The IC parts reminds me why I rolled my eyes and straight out passing over some IC texts in WOD books. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThis is urban fantasy, so we all know we'll need the &quot;hey rookie, seems you're now supernatural and facing a reality you thought never existed, let me tell you how not to get yourself killed by next week&quot; speech. <br /> <br /> But please, was it necessary for it to be spelled out by obnoxious, pseudo witty, pop culture referencing teenagers? <br /> <br /> And not just once, but five time, one for each family? <br /> <br /> <br /> Years ago, there was a guy attempting to make a vampire mmo solo (suicidal project clearly, and he did closed it eventually), he wrote a hell lot of IC lore dump and it's clear he was 100% influenced by the WOD. <br /> And outside of a few cringe worthy segments, it was far better than those five here. <br /> <br /> The dead mmo is Shadow's Kiss if someone wonder. <br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, the sorcerer presentation would have been better from an ex cultist/academician speaking with a more measured tone than &quot;it is worth it? Hell fucking yeah!&quot; <br /> <br /> Which is weird singe despite it's cringeness at time, wod books had good &quot;teach at a silent observer who's the reader's perspective&quot; types. <br /> <br /> <br /> -far too few explainations of how things works, mixed with contradictions<br /> <br /> Not in particular order:<br /> <br /> Which lineages can have members of different cursing origin. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bBy that I mean whenether the accursed is cursed by his own actions, by someone else, by lineage, etc<br /> <br /> -For the hungry for exemple, we're told that they can only get accursed by another hungry which feed them their lineage based special food. <br /> How does that work for the heirs who feed on hearts, do they feed their own to their &quot;childer&quot;? <br /> <br /> But we're also told that some lineages appeared spontaneously like the bathorite, was bathory accursed by another hungry or did she cursed herself?<br /> <br /> This is also contradicted by an entanglement 4 power wihich make a human temporary undead, and if they die in that way, they become accursed either as a dead or hungry, without the feeding by the maker. <br /> <br /> We also have no clue of how feeding works, at most the vorare section indicates that people without souls lost their most important part. <br /> <br /> We're also told IC (which truly is a point against continuing using IC explanations) that feeding requires a form of consent, something also implied int the heir section. But there's no mention of that anywhere else. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> -As above, we don't know how the &quot;feeding&quot; of the dead works, we also don't know how the dead obtain new bodies, since the only powers linked to possession seems to require a degree of willingness of the host<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> As opposed to the hungry and the outcast, it seems every lineage can be joined by self cursing, family cursing or cursing by someone/situation. <br /> <br /> The outcast section implies the lineage only involves either outsiders cursed to be amongs human or their descendants. But the chimera sections implies they were humans first, so can a human be cursed as a chimera? <br /> <br /> <br /> -the process of selecting a family is also confusing<br /> <br /> Is a sorcerer cursed to fuel his magic by sacrificing fame, ergo joining the faceless, or is it a choice they make? <br /> <br /> Same for the hungry, it seems the family choose the accursed by transforming him, but the black hearts implies a notion of choice.<br /> <br /> Same for the dead, apparently your family is typically those who found you first, does that me a dead can shift &quot;diet&quot; and join another family? <br /> <br /> <br /> In terms of rules, two things<br /> <br /> -the magic section is pretty confusing. A low entanglement you can only take spells from either your family/lineage group *or* if the specific lineage tag is part of the spell atunements. Which, At least for my personnal reading experience, was both confusing and, once understood, very hard to follow while reading it<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> -and here more a point of personnal preference, but I'm not sure I approve of the idea of putting only entanglement 1-4 in the core book. <br /> <br /> I'm of the philosophy that a game must be able to offer the whole experience in a corebook. Not split it in ever more buyable parts. <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T05:18:28-08:00","id":1545385,"title":"","content":"I'm slightly less bothered by the tone of the IC narrators than I am by the sheer volume of important information that's gated behind unreliable narrators. <br /> <br /> In terms of voice, I do agree that a lot of them have that 90s White Wolf too-cool-for-school vibe to them (quite literally in the case of Izzy). I think there's a general problem with IC narrators for Lineages in that because each Family is so different there's not really a single voice that fits the whole Lineage. A more academic / occultist tone makes sense for the Archivists but not for the Network, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T06:35:15-08:00","id":1545387,"title":"","content":"I would like a tiny bit more neutral and mechanical explanation for each damnation, like possession for the Dead, how do the Vorare eat souls or how Chimera interact with the mask for example but i'm not too bothered by the narration, I would like to see more example of how families interact with each others and other accursed families outside of their native lineage. I'm having some troubles trying to see how multiple families might form an accursed community in a given setting (or at least something that doesn't only rely on crews interacting with other crews)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T06:54:34-08:00","id":1545388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544814-some-hopefully-constructive-criticism-of-curseborne?p=1545387#post1545387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like a tiny bit more neutral and mechanical explanation for each damnation, like possession for the Dead, how do the Vorare eat souls or how Chimera interact with the mask for example but i'm not too bothered by the narration, I would like to see more example of how families interact with each others and other accursed families outside of their native lineage. I'm having some troubles trying to see how multiple families might form an accursed community in a given setting (or at least something that doesn't only rely on crews interacting with other crews)</div> </div> </div> </div>I just want to clarify here because it matters. <br /> <br /> When you say natural and mechanical explanation for each Damnation do you mean for each *lineage* or each *family*?<br /> <br /> I feel that pretty much every Family needs a sidebar explaining what its &quot;thing&quot; is in neutral, game-usable terms with a focus on what they mean to starting characters (so you don't wind up with the whole family writeup being about how you grant wishes or raise the dead and then have the devs explaining that actually granting wishes and raising the dead aren't the sort of thing low-entanglement PCs are meant to do).<br /> <br /> That means for each Hungry family: what is its feeding preference and how does it actual go about fulfilling it, where a feeding preference demonstrably involves using a supernatural ability what effects is it legitimate for that ability to have in actual play.<br /> <br /> For each Dead family: what is its Urge and does its urge require to instil the chosen emotion or metro be in the presence of it. Does Ghost feeding *drain* emotion (so you wind up less scared after a Poltergrist attack) or not? Does it actually make sense for Urges to be explained in terms of &quot;emotions&quot; at all. Vengeance isn't an emotion neither is whatever the Zeds are into. <br /> <br /> For each Primal family: what kind of forms do their Wild Forms take and what additional tools does the Storyguide have to make those forms feel impactful over and above a single Enhancement on Physical actions.<br /> <br /> For each Outcast family, what do their True Forms tend to look like, are they usually angelic or demonic or other, what kind of ability to manipulate Battlegrounds did the family have? If the Family has a unique supernatural thing they do like granting wishes, making devil's bargains or tending beautiful gardens, how can the SG work with the player to make that a reality?<br /> <br /> For each Sorcerer family, what kinds of things does it sacrifice, what do its rituals to sacrifice them look like and how ad hoc can they be (can an Unburdened carry a bunch of tiny pieces of handcrafted jewellery and sacrifice one whenever they need a CD for example). Where sacrificing involves doing something that they couldn't normally do (like destroying their own memories) how does that actually work?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T08:07:53-08:00","id":1545389,"title":"","content":"A good chunk of the IC dialog is definitely Gen X and older Millennials trying to sound like Zoomers and I did inwardly cringe a few times reading it.<br /> <br /> The phrase &quot;Don't get it twisted&quot; was used one too many times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T09:30:53-08:00","id":1545392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544814-some-hopefully-constructive-criticism-of-curseborne?p=1545389#post1545389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A good chunk of the IC dialog is definitely Gen X and older Millennials trying to sound like Zoomers and I did inwardly cringe a few times reading it.<br /> <br /> The phrase &quot;Don't get it twisted&quot; was used one too many times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Missed opportunity to have skibidi toilets as a major antagonist. <br /> <br /> I didn't even realise &quot;don't get it twisted&quot; was a zoomer thing. But yeah some of the narrators have quite intense &quot;hello, fellow kids&quot; energy. I mean Izzy, who was canonically born around 2007 uses *Predator* as a go-to cultural reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T09:00:12-08:00","id":1545473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544814-some-hopefully-constructive-criticism-of-curseborne?p=1545388#post1545388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just want to clarify here because it matters.<br /> <br /> When you say natural and mechanical explanation for each Damnation do you mean for each *lineage* or each *family*?<br /> <br /> I feel that pretty much every Family needs a sidebar explaining what its &quot;thing&quot; is in neutral, game-usable terms with a focus on what they mean to starting characters (so you don't wind up with the whole family writeup being about how you grant wishes or raise the dead and then have the devs explaining that actually granting wishes and raising the dead aren't the sort of thing low-entanglement PCs are meant to do).<br /> <br /> That means for each Hungry family: what is its feeding preference and how does it actual go about fulfilling it, where a feeding preference demonstrably involves using a supernatural ability what effects is it legitimate for that ability to have in actual play.<br /> <br /> For each Dead family: what is its Urge and does its urge require to instil the chosen emotion or metro be in the presence of it. Does Ghost feeding *drain* emotion (so you wind up less scared after a Poltergrist attack) or not? Does it actually make sense for Urges to be explained in terms of &quot;emotions&quot; at all. Vengeance isn't an emotion neither is whatever the Zeds are into.<br /> <br /> For each Primal family: what kind of forms do their Wild Forms take and what additional tools does the Storyguide have to make those forms feel impactful over and above a single Enhancement on Physical actions.<br /> <br /> For each Outcast family, what do their True Forms tend to look like, are they usually angelic or demonic or other, what kind of ability to manipulate Battlegrounds did the family have? If the Family has a unique supernatural thing they do like granting wishes, making devil's bargains or tending beautiful gardens, how can the SG work with the player to make that a reality?<br /> <br /> For each Sorcerer family, what kinds of things does it sacrifice, what do its rituals to sacrifice them look like and how ad hoc can they be (can an Unburdened carry a bunch of tiny pieces of handcrafted jewellery and sacrifice one whenever they need a CD for example). Where sacrificing involves doing something that they couldn't normally do (like destroying their own memories) how does that actually work?<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say a bit of bot.<br /> <br /> for example with the Hungry, i'd like to know if by drinking blood, must they murder a victim and drain them of all their blood ? Can they only take a little bit and if so does that impose a condition on their victims or some injury levels ? Is their &quot;kiss&quot; pleasurable like in VTM or VTR or is the act of drinking blood only painful to mortals ? But then for families like the Heir or the Iscariot, i don't need much confirmation that eating someone's heart or flesh is usually fatal.<br /> <br /> All in all i'd agree that maybe a small box next to each family that neutrally explain in game terms the specific of that particular family brand of damnation would be very, very helpful along with expending more in game terms on how each Damnation affect the new &quot;living&quot; state of an Accursed, (like how Matthew Dawkins mentioned in the Guide to the Nephilim that Outcasts don't age like normal people for example which is not indicated anywhere in the manuscript as far as i can see).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-12T13:36:38-08:00","id":1545753,"title":"","content":"As I'm building my own Lineage for fun, and thinking about how to do their own set of Practices, it occurs to me I'm not quite sold on how Powers in Curseborne work.<br /> <br /> On the surface, making a set of spells that can be purchased ala carte allows a player to just pick the things they want, the versatility of said spells being tied directly to Entanglement is where I'm starting to have some concerns.<br /> <br /> As it is, in most of the classic games, you had an ever escalating set of powers building upon one another in the dot system. Outside of Mages who had to increase their arete, and werewolves who had their gifts... Vampires, Wraiths, Changelings, Mummies, Mortal Numina, and pretty much everything else followed the progressive dot system.<br /> <br /> Curseborne on the other hand, ties the versatility and escalating 'dots' directly to the characters Power Stat, Entanglement. Which leads to the situation where in order to get the most supernatural might as quickly as possible, it's best for players to frontload into Entanglement as quickly as possible.<br /> <br /> Unlocking that higher level of Entanglement, then makes it easy to go back to those spells and purchase the higher and more powerful Entanglement uses of them.<br /> <br /> A similar situation happens in Mage to a smaller degree with characters wanting to increase their Arete/Gnosis, but every Sphere/Arcana dot comes with so much versatility and power inherently, players start focusing on broadening their abilities when they reach around Arete 3.<br /> <br /> I'm starting to think I would have preferred to have each spell be a 5 dot power, simply because it would make players less concerned with getting their Entanglement higher as quickly as possible.<br /> <br /> But perhaps I'm overthinking it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-12T19:05:03-08:00","id":1545763,"title":"","content":"Remember players don't have any control over when Entanglement increases, it's a pure plot device / milestone thing.<br /> <br /> I do think the way things are currently gated is weird, there are E4 powers that seem quite modest and base abilities that seem busted as hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T03:54:27-08:00","id":1545778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544814-some-hopefully-constructive-criticism-of-curseborne?p=1545763#post1545763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember players don't have any control over when Entanglement increases, it's a pure plot device / milestone thing.<br /> <br /> I do think the way things are currently gated is weird, there are E4 powers that seem quite modest and base abilities that seem busted as hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>.. <br /> <br /> So the power Stat is 100% arbitrary and up to the whims of the ST. I'd forgotten that. <br /> <br /> More and more this game is starting to seem like it really wants to be powered by the Apocalypse. This half way thing between story game mechanicss and traditional role-playing mechanics is a little frustrating. <br /> <br /> This is my fault for being not as familiar with Storypath as I am with Storyteller and Storytelling. <br /> <br /> I dislike how I'm coming down so negative, but there seems to be so much missing from Curseborne, like it's a half finished game that expects the ST to fill in all the blanks with hand waving. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T06:22:59-08:00","id":1545784,"title":"","content":"To be fair the Power Trait of other Storypath games are not \u201c100% arbitrary and up to the whims of the ST\u201d.<br /> <br /> Trinity has 3 different power traits (Inspiration, Quantum and Psi) and they are all bought with XP<br /> Scion has a system for Legend. For Heroes it is tied to the characters complete personal long and short aspirations and the group complete a group aspiration (Band Deeds). Demigods it is tied to the steps you need to go through to become a full God and for Gods it is related to you position in the pantheon (to reach maximum Legend you need to take over the pantheon or create your own).<br /> <br /> The system is solid for those games I played them and assure you. Can\u2019t say the same for Curseborne\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T06:48:29-08:00","id":1545786,"title":"","content":"To be double fair, relying heavily on GM fiat arguably *is* a traditional RPG mechanic. It's something that storygames tend to limit in my experience.<br /> <br /> That said I do think CB has a bit of a &quot;trad game with storygame trappings&quot; thing going on but fit me that's more things like having a success-with-consequences system but weirdly also having consequences for failure that are different, having a very open ended power system but also aggressively gating it, having a power stat at *all* when accumulating power doesn't seem to be the point of the game, not fully committing to NPCs and PCs following different game mechanics (a lot of spells, for example, seem to assume that NPC Accursed have PC stats), and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T08:18:40-08:00","id":1545789,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping we'll see some significant revisions or mechanical tune ups in the final product. I think there's a great game buried under the prototype that's the current version of Curseborne...<br /> <br /> But in it's current iteration it's a very limited game that doesn't seem capable of any long term campaigns or doing anything beyond &quot;Slice of life Supernatural adventures.&quot;<br /> <br /> Wandering beyond the very narrow fenced in scope of what's been presented will lead to lots of issues and or extra work load for the ST who will have to fill in the numerous blanks and mechanical problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T09:49:49-08:00","id":1545792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544814-some-hopefully-constructive-criticism-of-curseborne?p=1545789#post1545789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping we'll see some significant revisions or mechanical tune ups in the final product. I think there's a great game buried under the prototype that's the current version of Curseborne...<br /> <br /> But in it's current iteration it's a very limited game that doesn't seem capable of any long term campaigns or doing anything beyond &quot;Slice of life Supernatural adventures.&quot;<br /> <br /> Wandering beyond the very narrow fenced in scope of what's been presented will lead to lots of issues and or extra work load for the ST who will have to fill in the numerous blanks and mechanical problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you see as the limitations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T10:27:21-08:00","id":1545793,"title":"","content":"My opinion here. I think there is a problem here that is the effort was made to make it as wide as possible and gave little depth.<br /> You have the WoD lore that evolved with every book (I do t like it but ok), but also had a thick lore in the first edition books. The story of the vampires and the many clans interactions and the rise of Tremere as a small but powerful clan that made Camarilla needed to be protected by it for example.<br /> In the CoD has also a thick lore since the first book of each splat, not even touching the second edition that makes the lore even deeper. The setting is not generic, but it is open and have in\u00fameros hooks for all kinds of stories.<br /> CB tries to be equivalent to 1e, with open ended sand box setting, but it opens to soo many options that it is virtually impossible to cover many styles of play or open hooks.<br /> The prove of that is seen even by the devs. I never saw a post saying \u201cwhat can you play using \u2026\u201d. The games usually say \u201cyou are \u2026 and you are facing things like \u2026 , \u2026 and \u2026\u201d<br /> Take Trinity 1e. It is a huge and open setting, with all the possible sci-fi themes explored, but they made it in a way that if you don\u2019t know what to do, you have built in hooks: let\u2019s fight Aberrants; let\u2019s explore planets; let\u2019s explore the interaction of the organizations; etc.<br /> Curseborne points us to a teen drama about people that feel bad about being monsters while fighting people that are happy for being monsters. It\u2019s not that you can\u2019t explore it, see Buffy and Sabrina, but there are no big hood to hang some long and complex stories.<br /> <br /> TL;DR: so many options it gets shallow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T10:34:47-08:00","id":1545794,"title":"","content":"Expanding a little more. Part of that feeling is because it is a book where the setting is described in character, so their drama is the game drama.<br /> My family is a bunch of assholes.<br /> I hate I am cursed this way.<br /> Fuck the world I am cursed.<br /> <br /> If you try to step away from this ideas you are not covered. We have a very shallow vision of the complexities of the families. We have a shallow vision of the interaction of the legacies and families.<br /> <br /> I feel the 12yo me would love it for a few months and a few sessions, as I used to love to play VtM to kill people for their blood and to be bullet proof. But the 15yo me would say ok\u2026 boring\u2026 so what? And the 42yo me just read a few pages and don\u2019t even bother to buy it.<br /> <br /> Edit: not to mention the fact many things are left with no answers. The feeding process kills? Does ghosts need to feed their bodies? Can you switch families and embrace their traits or do you get the family but not the curse?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 11-13-2024, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T13:19:52-08:00","id":1545811,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m alright with how Entanglement enhances all of the spells. I think that mechanic is cool. It does make Entanglement pretty powerful, so it does put an obligation on the SG to let everybody increase their Entanglement at around the same rate.<br /> <br /> Something that does trouble me is the shallowness of some of the families, as Mateus discusses above. This kinda struck me while I was reading (and commenting on) some discussion about the Tzimisce and how complex they are, their history, the political dynamics between them and other Clans, etc. while there are numerous character options in Curseborne, more than the WoD in a lot of ways. But none of the factions seem to have that depth and nuance of, just as an example, the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> That, of course, is a little bit unfair. We\u2019ve had 30 years of world building that influences the Tzimisce, including 2 Clan Books, 2 Guides to the Sabbat, and countless other books that flesh them out. When V:tM 1st Edition came out, the Clans were a bit flag as well. I\u2019m hoping to see a bit more development on the families arise over time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T14:24:30-08:00","id":1545815,"title":"","content":"I did buy the 1e core books of VtM, WtA and MtAs and to be fair much of the things that were explored over the years were all there. Sure, Tremere were there because they were in the Ars Magica WW had bought the right to a some time earlier, but the other clans and the interaction and stories are there. It is fun that even the illustrations of a good part of the book are all about Cain and the first city.<br /> <br /> It would be unfair to compare CB to 3rd edition or even the second edition, but to the first book ever it\u2019s not an insult to say VtM 1e is far better than CB, just because it allow much more than teen drama. CB gives options that are not really deep, as far as I know you can pick any lineage and family and play in a group that should never exist for no reason they have to be together other than the players want to. You can say \u201cwhat about the conflict?\u201d And I say \u201cconflict is required for advancing the story when characters want to be together for a reason, as soon as they don\u2019t want to and don\u2019t need to, the group disbands\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T17:20:03-08:00","id":1545820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544814-some-hopefully-constructive-criticism-of-curseborne?p=1545792#post1545792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do you see as the limitations?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mateus has described it pretty well when he referred to it as &quot;High School Drama&quot;. I described it as &quot;Supernatural Slice of Life.&quot; That seems to be the default and only way the game is set to be played. &quot;You're a brand new cursed, you hate your family, (though we don't know why, since the information on families is very shallow) try to get by with your friends. Occasionally something creepy might show up in your neighborhood.&quot;<br /> <br /> There doesn't seem to be any direction to the game besides that. There's no political structure to interact with, whether to rebel or try and take it over. There's no great series of antagonists to be opposed. There's no Masquerade/Veil/Secrets to be kept from the mortals. There's no ancient mysteries to explore and unravel. There's no set Accursed social gatherings to mingle and schmooze. There's no places of power to actively seek, no resources to fight over.<br /> <br /> Heck there's no ability to actively seek greater power for yourself if you want to be all in on being Accursed.<br /> <br /> Right now it's mainly... the Primal goes to the bar and thanks to their damnation starts a fight and now the cops are involved...<br /> <br /> Which don't get me wrong, that *IS* Fun. But eventually, the Accursed will get to a point where they're not just focused on surviving day to day, night to night. They're going to be established, and no longer be worried about the small stuff.... Except the game doesn't seem to support that, it seems to want to focus entirely on the small stuff.<br /> <br /> I recently pledged to Kevin Crawford's &quot;Ashes without Numbers&quot; and in his talk of how to run Civilization collapsing games... he mentions most of the initial games will be focused just on survival. Trying to acquire resources, take care of regular problems... it's fun and dramatic... but eventually, survivors will reach a point where they've *SOLVED* those problems... and that's when the game changes to exploring and encountering other groups and organizations and dealing with them.<br /> <br /> Right now, Curseborne is just a game focused on that first part. You can only do so many street level personal plots before eventually you want something more... and in a game that's got such an interesting setting premise, the setting and rules being so limited in scope at the moment is disappointing.<br /> <br /> I've been thinking up larger, cross lineage Accursed Organizations and Secret Societies that would give more direction for characters than just &quot;I hate my family, I have to pay my bills, and I just ate my boyfriend's memories.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T17:49:57-08:00","id":1545821,"title":"","content":"Yeah, y\u2019all are right. Even in 1st edition VtM, without too much Clan background or history, there is a more vibrant setting - because there in fact is a setting. A Ventrue interacting with. Brujah seems inherently more meaningful and compelling than an Heir interacting with a Black Heart.<br /> <br /> The families could be more fleshed out, which they likely will be, but putting them into a compelling setting would be a major part of that. Will this change as the game progresses? Maybe so.<br /> <br /> Though I wonder how hard it would be to break free of the teen drama/slice of life model and do something a little more involved? Maybe not that hard, but would require more creativity on the SG\u2019s part. <br /> <br /> When I think of ideas that interest me regarding Curseborne, whether a a player or SG, I do find my mind turning to thoughts of fleshing out the setting, families, and political interconnections more than what we currently see.<br /> <br /> I also don\u2019t want to be too negative, there are certainly aspects of CB that really excite me, but all it takes is a quick glance at the VtM forums to make me realize that CB seems to be missing something. Maybe that something can be added though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T01:40:46-08:00","id":1545838,"title":"","content":"I mentioned in other threads that Curseborne feels like a very &quot;modern&quot; horror take on the subject of how gaming interacts with the supernatural. Present WOD is a bit stuck in the Nineties or trying to rebottle the zeitgeist of that time and it's moved on I believe. However, Curseborne feels like it nicely captures both the remake updates of several franchises of the past as well as adds their spin on things.<br /> <br /> Which TLDR, Curseborne is a gameline where you can play Resident Evil, Control, and Silent Hill just fine. You can play the heroic Curseborne up against a bunch of zombie-making mad scientists, you can play the player characters up against an incomprehensible extra-dimensional evil in a government building gone mad, and you could do a haunted town that conjures monsters from your guilt from killing your wife. You can be Leon Kennedy in this game or you can be James Sunderland.<br /> <br /> Right now, I feel like the game is a little too heavy on the extra-dimensional weirdness. The biggest most obvious antagonists are all &quot;Things from Beyond&quot; that are possessing your local shopping mall and turning the customers into faceless customers that mindlessly consume. That's not a complaint but just it got a lot of attention versus more locally grown threats. I don't think there's much in the way of teen drama as someone people have said as the game is very heavy on the Stephen King &quot;an alien thing is terrorizing this world's normality.&quot;<br /> <br /> Do I think it could use an Umbrella Corporation or Bureau of Control to provide some more Earthly threats and authority? Yes.<br /> <br /> But I'm sure that will come with time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T01:54:41-08:00","id":1545839,"title":"","content":"As mentioned by a few people, this is the first book in a game line, so we're not going to be presenting an established 30 year metaplot. I know that's obvious, but it bears repeating. It's not trying to be a game with that level of depth, at this time. It's a starter for people who want to find out more of the lore and a main course for people who want to develop their own. The core book has an entire chapter on life as an Accursed and at least two pages per Family, by my count, which is equal to the amount of content the clans received in a game like Vampire, except you have more options. Even more will come with future releases.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure where the idea of teen drama comes from other than our having one of the ready-made characters - Izzy - being a high schooler. If she's a strong enough character to make people here who have read the manuscript still think it's a teen drama/slice of life game (especially with the massive number of adversaries, setting locations, and story hooks in the book to counterbalance that), then I take it as high praise as I wrote her.<br /> <br /> Will there eventually be conspiracies and wider ranging threats in Curseborne? Absolutely. Not at this tier of gameplay, however, because the Curseborne core book is your gateway into the world and there are hundreds of stories you can tell with what's already in the book that involve your characters as individuals, your crew, and your Families. It'll definitely expand with time.<br /> <br /> All this said, I think the same points are being reiterated and they've been taken on board. Please submit feedback via the feedback form if there are changes you want to see in the core book, as posts in forums and Discords are easily lost to the mists of time. I'll now close this thread, as the criticisms have been made and I don't want this to turn into a series of bashing comments. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}